# Project Requirements Document

## Project Overview

**Project Name:** Hetri PAW (Pet Activity Wellness) Platform  
**Project Type:** Enterprise Facility Management Platform  
**Deployment:** Cross-Platform Desktop Application (Electron) with PostgreSQL Database  
**Architecture:** Multi-Role Enterprise System with Real-Time Capabilities  

Hetri PAW is a comprehensive facility management platform designed for pet care facilities offering TreatTap services. The platform supports multiple user roles including PAW Parents (customers), PAW Associates (staff), Facility Admins, and Hetri Admins, providing complete business management capabilities from customer booking to real-time analytics and multi-facility operations.

## Core Platform Requirements

### 1. Multi-Role User Management System

**PAW Parents (Customers):**
- Secure registration and profile management with pet information
- TreatTap session booking with real-time availability checking
- Live session viewing with MJPEG streaming (1-3 viewer limit per session)
- Real-time notifications via MQTT integration
- Session history and analytics tracking
- Payment processing and billing management
- Multi-pet profile management with preferences and medical history

**PAW Associates (Staff):**
- Staff authentication with facility-scoped access
- TreatTap session initiation and management tools
- Real-time customer communication via MQTT messaging
- Session monitoring with live camera feeds
- Customer interaction history and notes
- Scheduling and task management integration
- Performance analytics and reporting

**Facility Admins:**
- Comprehensive facility management dashboard
- Customer database with advanced search and filtering
- Pet profile management with medical history tracking
- Dynamic pricing configuration and management
- Real-time streaming analytics and camera monitoring
- ERP integration with financial and inventory tracking
- Staff scheduling and payroll management
- Business intelligence dashboard with live metrics

**Hetri Admins:**
- Multi-facility oversight and system management
- Global analytics and performance monitoring
- System health monitoring and maintenance tools
- User access control and permission management
- Platform configuration and feature management
- Advanced reporting and business intelligence

### 2. Database Architecture Requirements

**Primary Database: PostgreSQL 13+**
- Enterprise-grade relational database with ACID compliance
- 15+ interconnected tables with proper normalization
- UUID primary keys for security and scalability
- JSONB support for flexible data storage
- Connection pooling for optimal performance
- Automated backup and recovery procedures
- Migration management with rollback capabilities

**Core Database Tables:**
- Users (authentication and profile data)
- Facilities (multi-facility support with GPS coordinates)
- PAW Parents (customer-specific information)
- PAW Associates (staff profiles and permissions)
- Pets (pet profiles with medical history and preferences)
- TreatTap Sessions (session management with booking conflicts prevention)
- Camera Streams (streaming configuration and analytics)
- Bookings (scheduling with validation and conflict resolution)
- Notifications (real-time message management)
- Analytics (business intelligence and reporting data)
- ERP Integration (financial and inventory data)

**Secondary Services:**
- Redis Caching (session management and performance optimization)
- MQTT Message Queue (real-time communication)
- File Storage (image uploads and document management)

### 3. Authentication and Security Requirements

**Enterprise Security Framework:**
- bcrypt password hashing with salt rounds
- JWT token-based authentication with HTTP-only cookies
- Role-based access control (RBAC) with facility-scoped permissions
- Session management with automatic refresh tokens
- Secure logout with complete token invalidation
- Password complexity requirements and account lockout protection
- Two-factor authentication support for admin roles
- Audit logging for security events and user actions

**Data Protection:**
- GDPR compliance for customer data protection
- Encrypted data transmission (HTTPS/WSS)
- Secure file upload with virus scanning
- Personal data anonymization capabilities
- Data retention policies and automated cleanup
- Secure backup encryption and access controls

### 4. Real-Time Communication Requirements

**MQTT Integration (Sub-100ms Latency):**
- MQTT 5.3+ broker with QoS guarantees
- Facility-scoped topic namespacing for security isolation
- Device status monitoring and heartbeat management
- Automatic reconnection with exponential backoff
- Message throttling and rate limiting
- Real-time notifications for critical events
- Bi-directional communication for staff and customer interactions

**Data Polling Architecture:**
- 30-second interval polling for non-critical updates
- Conditional polling based on user activity and screen focus
- Optimized PostgreSQL queries for efficient data retrieval
- Error handling and retry logic for failed requests
- Bandwidth optimization for mobile and low-bandwidth connections

### 5. Video Streaming Requirements

**Professional Camera Integration:**
- MJPEG camera feed integration with quality adaptation
- Real-time stream monitoring and health checking
- 1-3 concurrent viewer limits per session with queue management
- Stream quality optimization based on bandwidth
- Recording capabilities for session documentation
- Privacy controls and access management

**Stream Distribution:**
- HLS (HTTP Live Streaming) for broad device compatibility
- CDN integration for scalable stream distribution
- Adaptive bitrate streaming for network optimization
- Stream analytics and viewer metrics
- Bandwidth monitoring and cost optimization
- Geographic content delivery optimization

